            <ArticleTitle>Radiology case of the month: recurrent knee pain in a young athlete.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>125-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 22-year-old male collegiate basketball player with a history of right knee pain presents with pain and swelling of his right knee. Physical exam reveals local swelling and tenderness over the right proximal tibial-fibular joint.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
